From: xmrblocks security audit <security@monerofund.org>
Subject: [PATCH 0002] finding 4: bounds-check real_output before indexing the ring

tx_source.real_output is a size_t taken straight from the deserialised blob and
was used to index tx_source.outputs with no check, in both the unsigned-tx and
signed-tx paths of /checkandpush.

The read is not merely out of bounds, it is disclosed: on the OUTPUT_DNE path
the value read is formatted into the response body ("Output with amount X and
index Y does not exist!"), which reaches the client via main.cpp. Because
sizeof(output_entry) is 72 = 8*9 and 9 is invertible mod 2^64, every 8-byte
aligned offset is reachable in both directions, making this an arbitrary
aligned 64-bit read of the address space, one word per request.

Note the fix REJECTS rather than clamps. Clamping or skipping would let a
tx_source with an empty `outputs` vector through to
construct_mstch_mixin_timescales(), which dereferences min_element() on the
resulting empty mixin group (finding 22), and to mark_real_mixins_on_timescales()
(finding 6). Those two are currently unreachable only because this code path
faults first.

Reproducers: poc/micro/f04_f05_oob_read.cpp (ASan), f04c_arbitrary.cpp
(recovers a planted secret exactly), poc/http/f04_solve_offset.py.
---
diff --git a/src/page.h b/src/page.h
index 5eed1e1..6006e2b 100644
--- a/src/page.h
+++ b/src/page.h
@@ -2913,10 +2913,27 @@ show_checkrawtx(string raw_tx_data, string action)
 
                     //cout << "tx_source.real_output: "             << tx_source.real_output << endl;
                     //cout << "tx_source.real_out_tx_key: "         << tx_source.real_out_tx_key << endl;
                     //cout << "tx_source.real_output_in_tx_index: " << tx_source.real_output_in_tx_index << endl;
 
+                    // real_output indexes `outputs` and arrives from the
+                    // submitted blob. Reject rather than clamp: clamping would
+                    // let a malformed source reach the timescale code below,
+                    // which cannot cope with an empty mixin group.
+                    if (tx_source.real_output >= tx_source.outputs.size())
+                    {
+                        string out_msg = fmt::format(
+                                "Real output index {:d} is out of range "
+                                "({:d} ring members)",
+                                tx_source.real_output,
+                                tx_source.outputs.size());
+
+                        cerr << out_msg << endl;
+
+                        return string(out_msg);
+                    }
+
                     uint64_t index_of_real_output = tx_source.outputs[tx_source.real_output].first;
 
                     tx_out_index real_toi;
 
                     uint64_t tx_source_amount = (tx_source.rct ? 0 : tx_source.amount);
@@ -3296,10 +3313,22 @@ show_checkrawtx(string raw_tx_data, string action)
 
             for (const tx_source_entry&  tx_source: ptx.construction_data.sources)
             {
                 transaction real_source_tx;
 
+                if (tx_source.real_output >= tx_source.outputs.size())
+                {
+                    string out_msg = fmt::format(
+                            "Real output index {:d} is out of range "
+                            "({:d} ring members)",
+                            tx_source.real_output, tx_source.outputs.size());
+
+                    cerr << out_msg << endl;
+
+                    return string(out_msg);
+                }
+
                 uint64_t index_of_real_output = std::get<0>(tx_source.outputs[tx_source.real_output]);
 
                 uint64_t tx_source_amount = (tx_source.rct ? 0 : tx_source.amount);
 
                 tx_out_index real_toi;
